       --iiss, --iipp, --iisspp
           These options are ignored for compatibility with older versions of
           the dpkg build scripts but are now deprecated. Previously they were
           used to tell ddppkkgg--ggeennccoonnttrrooll to include the Section and Priority
           fields in the control file. This is now the default behaviour. If
           you want to get the old behaviour you can use the --UU option to
           delete the fields from the control file.

       --PP_p_a_c_k_a_g_e_-_b_u_i_l_d_-_d_i_r
           Scan _p_a_c_k_a_g_e_-_b_u_i_l_d_-_d_i_r instead of ddeebbiiaann//ttmmpp.  This value is used
           to find the default value of the IInnssttaalllleedd--SSiizzee substitution
           variable and control file field, and for the default location of
           the output file.

       --OO[_f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e]
           Print the control file to standard output (or _f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e if
           specified, since dpkg 1.17.2), rather than to
           ddeebbiiaann//ttmmpp//DDEEBBIIAANN//ccoonnttrrooll (or _p_a_c_k_a_g_e_-_b_u_i_l_d_-_d_i_r//DDEEBBIIAANN//ccoonnttrrooll if
           --PP was used).

       --??, ----hheellpp
           Show the usage message and exit.

       ----vveerrssiioonn
